.TH ORG 1 "August 2026" "org (organise)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
org \- Automatically sort and move files into designated directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B org
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B org
is a fast, C++ based command-line tool that automatically organizes files in a directory based on predefined rules. It supports regex matching, extension grouping, and continuous watching using inotify.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Simulate actions without actually doing them.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Scan directories recursively.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Display detailed execution output.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-auto\-rename
Automatically rename conflicting files without prompting the user.
.TP
.BR \-\-conflict=\fIMODE\fR
Set conflict strategy. Valid modes are: \fIrename\fR, \fIskip\fR, or \fIoverwrite\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Watch the directory continuously and organise new files as they are created or moved in.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config=\fIFILE\fR
Use a specific configuration file instead of the default paths.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-undo
Undo the last batch of moves, using the history log.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the project's version and exit.
